{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He spoke.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] asked: why were Bezalel and Oholiab chosen? And he answered that Bezalel was of the tribe of Judah, whom Jacob likened to a lion's cub, and Oholiab was of the tribe of Dan, whom Moses likened to a lion's cub, and the lion narrows from behind — and so the Temple was [wider at the front, narrower at the rear]. But this is the homily of the homilist, for Bezalel and Oholiab did not build the Temple, and the width of the tabernacle they made was uniform, and there is no substance to his question, for they were chosen because there was none in Israel like them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Read 'והשיב' as introducing Saadia's own answer to his own question. The phrase 'וזה דרש הדורש' marks Ibn Ezra's dismissal of the homiletic reading; 'הבית' taken as the Temple, per the lion-geometry midrash context."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:34.497798617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}